fix(api): repair three public APIs broken by the contact-details grant change

The contact-details hardening (team_workspaces / federations / rinks)
revoked table-level SELECT from anon + authenticated and re-granted it
PER COLUMN. That fixed the privacy leak, but it silently broke every
PUBLIC read that used select('*') on those tables:

  /api/teams   HTTP 500  permission denied for table team_workspaces
  /api/rinks   HTTP 500  permission denied for table rinks
  /api/pwhl    HTTP 500  permission denied for table team_workspaces

PostgREST validates a star select against the column grants, even when
head:true, so `select('*', { count: 'exact', head: true })` fails too.
tsc and the build were both green throughout — the select is a string and
the grant is a database fact.

Fixed by naming the columns explicitly:
  /api/teams  — full public team column list + leagues(name)
  /api/rinks  — full public rink column list (contact columns excluded,
                which is the point of the hardening)
  /api/pwhl   — full public team column list + leagues(name)
  src/app/page.tsx and src/lib/country-page.ts — count selects now use
  select('id', { count: 'exact', head: true })

Also audited every anon-client select on the three revoked tables: 69
selects total, of which only these used a star. The other 65 name their
columns and were unaffected.

Gate 14 (_audit-embed-columns.mjs) now also fails on any anon
select('*') against a table whose table-level SELECT is revoked, so this
class cannot come back. It found two more while being written (a real
count select on src/app/page.tsx, and a doc comment in
src/lib/supabase.ts that would have taught the next developer the broken
pattern).

The post-deploy smoke test now checks /api/teams, /api/rinks and
/api/pwhl too, so an embed or grant change that breaks a JSON route is
caught within minutes of the deploy instead of at the next audit.
